From cc882a7b1dc8c509f6e7bbc9d3cc30795a937d5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alex <49746433+Master-Yoba@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 11:34:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] cpu: run ahead-of-time recompiled guest code from DLLs
 (SSD_AOT)

Modules recompiled to C++ by ss-delta's recomp/ and built as DLLs are
loaded from SSD_AOT (';'-separated paths) and checked against guest
memory with a code hash (the words the loader patches for variable
imports excluded). The JIT ends every block that reaches a recompiled
function's entry (PreCodeReadHook) and halts with UserDefined7;
DynarmicCPU::run copies the registers into the native context, calls the
function and continues where it returned.

Native code calls back through four hooks: call_indirect (native target,
or a nested JIT loop with lr set to a sentinel block), call_import (HLE
directly for svc stubs, the JIT for anything else), escape and
unsupported (a C++ exception caught at the innermost boundary; the JIT
continues there). A thread that exits while native frames are on its
stack unwinds them (CPUState::aot_unwind). HLE calls made inside run()
keep the caller's halted/break_ state (guest callbacks end on WFI).
Guest threads get 64 MiB host stacks while AOT is enabled.

Debugging and measurement: SSD_AOT_COUNT=1 (instruction counts on both
sides, JIT profile by entry), SSD_AOT_STATS=<file>, SSD_AOT_RANGE (which
functions run natively), SSD_AOT_TRACE=N, SSD_AOT_DUMP=<file>, and
SSD_AOT_DIFF=N, a differential mode that runs every Nth native call on a
shadow JIT first (journaled writes, undone) and compares registers and
memory.

Without SSD_AOT nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
